From 4e51434ed18e3dae3b7821b25eae668eaa783a7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:02:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Blaze 3.x heat2: send UserAuthenticated(8) so login
 completes

THE login-completion gate for heat2 (NHL 15 / Madden 25). After ps3Login
the real EA SDK blocks until the server pushes the LOCAL user's session as
UserSessions NotifyUserAuthenticated (Id 8); NotifyUserAdded (2) is only for
foreign personas. Without it the client showed "connecting to the EA
servers", pinged, then logged out.

Now sends the real EA post-login notification set in order: UserAuthenticated
(8) -> UserAdded (2) -> UserUpdated (5). Shapes reverse-engineered from the
FIFA 17 PS3 EBOOT (ceinydO/fifa17-ps3-online).

Live result (NHL 15, RPCS3): login now completes -- client sends postAuth,
updateNetworkInfo and the full online bootstrap (Messaging, AssociationLists,
Clubs, OSDK_TICKER/ARENA config); online music ticker plays; "connecting"
spinner replaced by "Retrieving data from server". Was: instant "EA servers
not available".

Known gap: a later PPU null-deref while retrieving data -- a game component
(2249/2250/2251/21/10) gets our empty response where it expects populated data.

1CON omitted from UserSessionLoginInfo: TdfUtils.EncodeTdfTag mis-encodes
digit-leading tags (writes 'Q' for '1'); value defaults to 0 anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
